1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,700
Most websites still assume one cursor: yours.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:08,445
When AI helps, its work is often hidden behind a chat box.

3
00:00:08,795 --> 00:00:12,500
Second Cursor proposes a new interaction model.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,087
The human and the agent share the same live surface,
at the same time.

5
00:00:16,437 --> 00:00:19,900
In Moving Day, the white cursor expresses taste.

6
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:25,902
The blue cursor makes the Agent's intent visible:
what it targets, why it moves, and when it waits.

7
00:00:26,252 --> 00:00:29,600
This is not chain of thought.

8
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:36,257
It is actionable disclosure: intent, progress, changes,
constraints, and when control returns to the human.

9
00:00:36,607 --> 00:00:42,200
The Agent can inspect the room, point out a problem,
and move or rotate unlocked furniture.

10
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:47,461
Every action happens through six structured WebMCP tools
connected to the live page.

11
00:00:47,811 --> 00:00:51,100
But authority stays human.
Lock an object and the Agent must preserve it.

12
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:54,300
Grab an item and the Agent yields.

13
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,843
When two choices are equally valid,
the Agent asks instead of guessing.

14
00:00:59,193 --> 00:01:04,209
Second Cursor turns AI from an invisible operator
into an understandable collaborator.

15
00:01:04,559 --> 00:01:06,790
One workspace. Two cursors.
